  "title": "Backfill a range of partitions from the asset drawer",
  "summary": "On a partitioned DuckLake asset, the Backfill button opens a range picker that previews which partitions are missing, failed or materialized, then re-runs the producing script once per partition with an explicit partition argument. Runs are sequential and idempotent, a failed partition does not stop the rest, and progress streams in the dialog and drawer header. Range backfill is an Enterprise feature; single-partition runs stay available in all editions.",
